                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued November 1 at 4:58PM MST until November 2 at 1:00AM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "FFWFGZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Flagstaff has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nMoenkopi Wash in Coconino County in north central Arizona...\n\n* Until 100 AM MST Monday.\n\n* At 458 PM MST, a gauge on the Moenkopi Wash reported a rise above\naction stage from heavy rain in the Moenkopi Wash basin. Further\nrises are expected, with water levels expected to exceed major\nflood stage. Flash flooding is already occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Heavy rain producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...River gauge reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of Moenkopi Wash.\n\n* For Moenkopi Wash near Tuba City:\nAt 4:45pm MST the stage was 26.0 feet.\nFlood Stage is 27.0 feet.\nForecast: A crest of 29.45 feet is expected at 5:00am MST Monday.\nImpacts:\nAt 27.0 feet: At 27.0 feet water begins to encroach on homes in\nlower Moenkopi Village and floods crop fields along the river.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nMoenkopi.\n\nThis includes the following creeks, washes and rivers...\nFivemile Wash, Hamblin Wash, Begashibito Wash and Moenkopi Wash.",
                "instruction": "Flooding of washes and creeks will occur, some dirt roads will become\nmuddy and impassable. Paved roads and underpasses could become\nflooded as well.\n\nStay away or be swept away! The banks of creeks and washes are\nunstable and unsafe during any flooding event.\n\nLow water crossings will become dangerous in heavy rain. Do not\nattempt to cross flooded roads. Find an alternate route.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
